# Reference copy

When writing or editing Basement UI reference content (`index.html`, `reference/`), describe what users see — not how it is built.

## Do

- Use component and design terms: “Pinned header”, “Striped rows”, “Optional tally”.
- Name tokens from the palette and type scale when relevant: “Gray D”, “XS”, “1rem”.
- Keep `sample-meta-label` and `sample-meta-detail` readable to designers and PMs.

## Do not

- Mention CSS class names, BEM modifiers, or HTML structure (`table--sticky`, `sidebar-item-meta`, `tag--filled`).
- Wrap implementation identifiers in `<code>`.
- Reference file paths, selectors, or props unless the page is explicitly a developer API doc.

## Examples

- Bad: `Scrollable body · table-wrap--scroll · table--sticky`
- Good: `Scrollable body · Pinned header and footer`

- Bad: `Uses sidebar-item-icon and tag--xs`
- Good: `Leading icon · Optional filled tag`
